        "conclusion": "## Before you spend the ad budget\n\nEligibility here is conditional, not categorical — it depends on your advertiser type, your product category, your target geography, your certification status, and what your destination page actually says, checked against each platform's current policy rather than last year's version of it. None of that review guarantees an approved campaign, but skipping it is how suppliers end up paying to find out the hard way.\n\n*Editorial Note on Diagram:* The accompanying graphic depicts an advertising compliance dashboard displaying a green checkmark for Meta. Note that Meta's published advertising policies do NOT define a dedicated commercial-laboratory peptide supplier category. Eligibility on Meta remains unconfirmed in public documentation and must be verified directly with Meta before campaign launch. RUO labeling does not constitute an advertising exemption on either network.\n\nIf you want a second set of eyes on your ad messaging, landing pages, or policy positioning before you launch a restricted-product campaign, [reach out to Belk Digital](/en/contact) to talk through a pre-launch website and campaign review.\n\n### Primary Documentation & Authoritative Resources\n- [Google Ads Policy: Pharmaceutical Manufacturers](https://support.google.com/adspolicy/answer/15597836?hl=en) — Official rules and certification for suppliers of antibodies, peptides, and compounds.\n- [Google Ads Policy: Healthcare and Medicines](https://support.google.com/adspolicy/answer/176031) — Overview of global restrictions on prescription medicines and speculative therapies.\n- [Google Ads Policy: Unapproved Pharmaceuticals and Supplements](https://support.google.com/adspolicy/answer/2423645) — Reference directory of disallowed substances and claims.\n- [Google Ads Application Process: Products & Services Certification](https://support.google.com/adspolicy/answer/16114090) — Official portal for child-account advertising certificates.\n- [Meta Transparency Center: Advertising Standards Overview](https://transparency.meta.com/policies/ad-standards/) — Core governance framework for commercial promotions.\n- [Meta Advertising Policy: Drugs and Pharmaceuticals](https://transparency.meta.com/policies/ad-standards/restricted-goods-services/drugs-pharmaceuticals/) — Public criteria for prescription, OTC, and online pharmacy promotions."
