            "conclusion": "Visibility in AI search is grounded in sound engineering and substantive content: making sure crawlers can access your pages without friction and providing clear, verifiable information that both human readers and automated synthesis engines can trust. As search interfaces evolve, organizations that maintain technical accessibility, transparent authorship, and authoritative content will sustain their visibility across traditional and generative search platforms alike.\n\nTo audit your website's crawler accessibility, structured data, and search performance, explore [Belk Digital's SEO optimization services](https://www.belkdigital.com/en/services/seo-optimization).\n\n### Primary Documentation and Official Sources\n- [Google Search Central: AI Features and Google Search](https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/ai-features)\n- [Google Search Central: Google Search Essentials](https://developers.google.com/search/docs/essentials)\n- [OpenAI: Overview of OpenAI Crawlers](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/bots)\n- [OpenAI: ChatGPT Search Guidance](https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9237897-chatgpt-search)\n- [Perplexity AI: Perplexity Crawlers Documentation](https://docs.perplexity.ai/docs/resources/perplexity-crawlers)\n- [Perplexity AI: How Perplexity Follows robots.txt](https://www.perplexity.ai/help-center/en/articles/10354969-how-does-perplexity-follow-robots-txt)\n- [Microsoft Bing: Webmaster Guidelines](https://www.bing.com/webmasters/help/webmaster-guidelines-30fba23a)\n- [Microsoft Bing: URL Inspection Tool](https://www.bing.com/webmasters/help/URL-Inspection-55a30305)\n- [IndexNow: Instant Indexing Protocol Documentation](https://www.indexnow.org/documentation)"
