            intro: 'Your website looks fine. Traffic is steady. Yet the contact form stays quiet, the cart keeps getting abandoned, and every quarterly review circles back to the same uncomfortable question: if the site looks good, why is nobody converting?\n\nThat gap between appearance and performance is where most web design trends content fails business owners. Search "web design trends" and you will find gorgeous listicles about bold typography, brutalist layouts, and animated cursors — with almost nothing about whether any of it moves revenue. Meanwhile, the design decisions that genuinely change conversion rate, search visibility, and customer trust rarely make the trend roundups at all, because they are structural rather than photogenic.\n\nThis guide sorts the difference. Instead of listing trends by name, we organize them by business outcome: which web design trends improve conversion rate, which expand accessibility and reach, which strengthen SEO performance, and which are purely aesthetic (plus the specific cases where those are still worth the budget). You will also get a decision framework for evaluating any new trend, a redesign sequence that protects existing rankings, and the questions worth asking before you hire a web design agency.',
